Table: Weather

+---------------+---------+
| Column Name   | Type    |
+---------------+---------+
| id            | int     |
| recordDate    | date    |
| temperature   | int     |
+---------------+---------+
id is the column with unique values for this table.
There are no different rows with the same recordDate.
This table contains information about the temperature on a certain day.
 

Write a solution to find all dates' id with higher temperatures compared to its previous calendar dates (yesterday).

SELECT today.id FROM weather as today
WHERE EXISTS
    (SELECT 1 FROM weather as yesterday
    WHERE today.temperature > yesterday.temperature
     AND DATEDIFF(today.recordDate, yesterday.recordDate) = 1);

Note : Inner Query has access to Outer Query table but not vice-versa.
